  <data name="NotificationsPage_StopReportNote.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>When enabled, the client controls when notifications are sent. Once playback reaches the watched threshold in “Playback behavior” (using the Chinese animation threshold for Chinese animation), or you manually select “Mark as watched”, the client reports “Playback stopped” to the server so that its configured notifications, such as forwarding to MoviePilot, are sent immediately. Seeking directly into this range also counts. Manually marking an item as watched reports 100% progress. Playback continues uninterrupted. This report is sent only once per playback session; no further progress reports or second stop report are sent for that session. This is a local setting, separate from the server notification list below.</value>
